{"id":"guardia_n","lemma":"guardián","pos":"noun","rank":2967,"glosses":["guardian, warden (person who guards or protects something)","guardian (superior in a Franciscan monastery)"],"ipa":"/ɡwaɾˈdjan/","gender":"m","forms":{"plural":"guardianes","feminine":"guardiana","femininePlural":"guardianas"},"examples":[{"text":"Necesitamos un perro guardián.","en":"We need a watchdog.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/275227","words":[{"g":"to need","l":"necesitar"},{"g":"a"},{"g":"dog"},null]},{"text":"¿Quién nos guardará de nuestros guardianes?","en":"Who'll protect us from our guardians?","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/831192","words":[{"g":"who"},{"g":"us"},{"g":"to save","l":"guardar"},{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"our, ours, to us","l":"nuestro"},null]},{"text":"Un perro que está siempre ladrando no es un buen perro guardián.","en":"A dog that barks all the time doesn't make a good watch dog.","audio":"https://tatoeba.org/en/audio/download/610788","words":[{"g":"a"},{"g":"dog"},{"g":"that"},{"g":"to be","l":"estar"},{"g":"always"},{"g":"to bark","l":"ladrar"},{"g":"no / not"},{"g":"to be","l":"ser"},{"g":"a"},null,{"g":"dog"},null]}]}